content.text:
SiteHeader used in both places. Adding a toggle there gives a visible button on both form and results. That seems good.

But careful: in the form page, the header is inside the sheet; adding a button aligned right. In results sidebar, wordmark + button row.

Implement SiteHeader as client component with useSettings toggle. Should the button show sun or moon? Icon shows the action or current state? Common: show moon when in light (click to go dark), sun when dark (click to go light). aria-label describes action. I'll expose icons: dark ? Sun : Moon, aria-label "Switch to light mode"/"Switch to night mode".

Also user said "add a button to toggle it" — maybe they want a button somewhere persistent (fixed top-right), like the settings gear fixed bottom-right. SiteHeader is inside the sheet and results; a fixed top-right button would be present everywhere including presentation. Hmm. The settings gear is fixed. A dedicated night-mode button likely near settings gear, or in header.

I think the header is the most natural. But on the results view the header is in the sidebar. Fine.

Also keep the settings menu checkbox? Having both is redundant but fine — settings shows "Following system" state; the button is a quick toggle. Keep both.

Button styling: match the compact look. Use `type="button"`, `title` maybe. Use lucide-react icons already dependency.

Let's write site-header.tsx:

```tsx
"use client";

import { Moon, Sun } from "lucide-react";

import { updateSettings, useSettings } from "@/lib/settings";
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";
import { Wordmark } from "@/components/wordmark";

export function SiteHeader({ className }: { className?: string }) {
  const { dark } = useSettings();
  const Icon = dark ? Sun : Moon;
  return (
    <header className="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <Wordmark className={cn("text-2xl", className)} />
      <button
        type="button"
        aria-label={dark ? "Switch to light mode" : "Switch to night mode"}
        aria-pressed={dark}
        onClick={() => updateSettings({ mode: dark ? "light" : "dark" })}
        className="flex size-9 shrink-0 cursor-pointer items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-border text-foreground transition-colors outline-none hover:bg-muted focus-visible:ring-3 focus-visible:ring-ring/50"
      >
        <Icon className="size-4" aria-hidden />
      </button>
    </header>
  );
}
```

Note SiteHeader is imported in a client component only, so "use client" fine. But presentation deck uses Wordmark directly, no header.

Check the form header layout: it's inside flex-col gap-12 section; header now full width. Good.

Run lint/typecheck.

